sentences.l:
He spoke, and, leaning back, he fell on his back, and then
lay bending-aslant his thick neck, and down him sleep
took, all-subduing;

And as when a man, a smith, an axe great or an adze
in water cold dips, loudly shrieking,
tempering it;

‘If indeed no one does violence to you, being alone,
a sickness, at least, it is not at all possible to escape, of great Zeus;
but you, for your part, pray to father Poseidon the lord.’

But I was planning how it might come about, best by far,
if for my companions some release from death and for me myself
I might find;

These silently I bound together with well-twisted withies,
on which the Cyclops slept, the monster, lawless things knowing,
three together taking;

but I for my part—
for there was a ram, of the flocks by far the best of all,
having taken him by the back, under the shaggy belly curled,
lay;

When early-born appeared, rose-fingered Dawn,
then thereafter to the pasture rushed out the male flocks,
and the females bleated, unmilked, about the pens;

And the lord, by pains, evil ones,
worn down, of all the sheep felt over the backs,
standing upright;

and first to the streams of the rivers you come,
and first to the stall you long to go back
at evening;
